Z||000002||rogergarrison||10-11-2001||02:39 PM||||Its different, eye catching. But being a painter for 30+ years, this guys got way more money than sense. For that price he could have had it gold plated and still had change. Personally, I think hes embellishing what he paid, maybe more like $15,000, and I think even that is stretching it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||10-11-2001||03:02 PM||||The dolphins are very well done, but on a red car with flames?<P>What's the best is the guy is hyping the car much like Mrs Illinois '96 has known to do.  So the paintjob was done by a world renowned marine artist Christian Lassen.  I like how he says that the paintjob could be worth as much as $300,000 since some previous artwork has gone for as much as $200,000.<P>If anyone buys this car from the forum, I want to collect the measly $15,000 and start on my next Fiero so please tell the guy I sent you if you buy it.<P>Thanks  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
